                    {
                        "sense_id": "41cbd265-a21e-3363-bd4a-8cf15caa686d",
                        "entry_id": "67f3076b-160c-37c1-8b40-dff67983498f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Which consoles."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca5d7a72-facf-44df-85ee-330fcdcc4567",
                                "sense_id": "41cbd265-a21e-3363-bd4a-8cf15caa686d",
                                "text": "[…] where in he reporteth of the coragius\nwordes that were moch consolatory […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a8bc39d-d76e-4f3e-b8de-20e7749de96e",
                                "sense_id": "41cbd265-a21e-3363-bd4a-8cf15caa686d",
                                "text": "1649, John Donne, Fifty Sermons, London: M.F., J. Marriot and R. Royston, Volume 2, “Sermon XVII. Preached at Lincolns Inne,” p. 140,\nWhere then is the restorative, the consolatory nature of these words? In this, beloved, consists our comfort […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a9e04ce-4a0c-4b09-a141-64d5cbba450b",
                                "sense_id": "41cbd265-a21e-3363-bd4a-8cf15caa686d",
                                "text": "The punishment of real tyrants is a noble and awful act of justice; and it has with truth been said to be consolatory to the human mind."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19380ea8-d2c8-4d92-bdcb-a43ae411142e",
                                "sense_id": "41cbd265-a21e-3363-bd4a-8cf15caa686d",
                                "text": "“It is singularly reviving after such hurricanes to feel calm return, and from the opening clouds to receive a consolatory gleam, softly testifying that the sun is not quenched.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "81b1463b-9ca0-4ddb-bb4b-420e3e9b21f8",
                                "sense_id": "41cbd265-a21e-3363-bd4a-8cf15caa686d",
                                "text": "Supper had been eaten, the turkey had been trussed, the children at last persuaded into their beds. That was the consolatory side of family life, Grorley thought—the long, Olympian codas of the emotions were cut short by the niggling detail."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
